.TH ELAN-GUARDIAN 8 "July 2026" "elan-guardian 0.2.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
elan-guardian \- diagnose and recover Elantech I2C input controllers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elan-guardian status
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B elan-guardian record
.B --output
.I TRACE.json
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B elan-guardian analyze
.I TRACE.json
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B elan-guardian recover
.RI [ --all " | " --device " I2C-ID]"
.RI [ --rebind ]
.br
.B elan-guardian watch
.RI [ --affected-only ]
.RI [ --interval-ms " MS]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B elan-guardian
captures Elantech IRQ and evdev evidence without grabbing an input device or
creating a virtual device. When expected movement is requested, it separates a
transport stall from a driver, userspace, or compositor fault.
.PP
Recovery is restricted to devices already bound to the
.B elan_i2c
kernel driver. An in-place kernel recovery attribute is preferred when present.
If it fails, the driver is unbound and rebound with bounded retries. The
.B --rebind
option requests that fallback directly.
.PP
The supplied kernel patch also provides a runtime health watchdog. It is armed
only while an Elan input node is open, checks the live transport every five
seconds, and performs in-place recovery after a failed probe or repeated report
errors. The watchdog is enabled by default on Lenovo ThinkPad P53 systems and
may be enabled for other validated systems with the
.B elan,runtime-watchdog
firmware property.
.PP
The packaged source in
.I /usr/src/elan-guardian-0.2.1/rust-shim
builds a replacement
.B elan_i2c.ko
whose packet decoder, watchdog policy, and recovery state machine are written
in no_std Rust. A narrow C shim supplies the Linux I2C, input, IRQ, power, and
module-registration ABI. The resulting module does not require CONFIG_RUST.
.SH RECORDING
Use
.B --expect-motion
only while deliberately moving the touchpad or TrackPoint during the capture.
Add
.B --cursor-stalled
when evdev activity is expected but the graphical cursor is not responding.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/elan-guardian-resume.service
runs one narrow recovery after resume on affected ThinkPad P53 systems whose
kernels do not yet contain the watchdog patch.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/elan-guardian-watch.service
monitors only the kernel recovery counter and escalates an in-place recovery to
a driver rebind. It never opens or grabs an evdev node.
.TP
.I /usr/src/elan-guardian-0.2.1/rust-shim
contains the Rust-core kernel module source and external Kbuild file.
.SH SECURITY
The recording path opens evdev read-only and never issues EVIOCGRAB. Recovery
requires root and validates both the I2C identifier and current driver binding.
